lyrics:
There is no fear,
Jesus took it away;
There is no fear,
Jesus hath set me free;
There is no fear,
Jesus is my trust;
There is no fear,
Jesus is my Shepherd.

CHORUS: Christ Jesus is a friend forever,
Christ Jesus never will leave me,
Jesus alone is all in all to me,
His love shall ever uphold me.

Upon a cross Jesus forgave me;
Upon a cross,
His blood He shed;
Upon a cross,
Jesus blotted out my guilt;
Upon a cross,
Jesus died for me.

Fountain of love,
Forever Christ is;
Fountain of love,
That taketh away my pain;
Fountain of love,
That taketh away my sorrows;
Fountain of love,
That filleth the heart.

Glory to Jesus,
For His divine love;
Glory to Jesus,
Throughout eternity.
Glory to Jesus,
For His tender mercy;
Glory to Jesus,
Our blessed God.

/:/ My righteousness is in the heavens, /:/
And from thence it shall come to me;
/:/ If in this world I have no shelter, /:/
The testimony of God shall have it.

CHORUS: We must wait
Upon the justice of God;
We are not alone here upon the earth;
Our refuge is Jehovah.

/:/ The sorrows that rise in the soul /:/
Christ can take away;
/:/ It mattereth not that they be grievous, /:/
The testimony of God I shall have.

/:/ In the Christian life there is suffering, /:/
Yet for a life to come;
/:/ If Jesus Christ suffered for my sake, /:/
Then why should I not also suffer?

There is a good seed
That sprang up at the dawn,
It fell into good ground
And straightway it could grow;
I am a seed of Christ,
Whom He chose by His power;
If my Lord help me,
I also shall be able to grow.

CHORUS: Leave me not, O Lord,
For I would be faithful unto Thee;
Unto the place whence I came forth,
I nevermore would return;
Remember me this day,
Suffer me not to perish.

There was also the seed
That sprang up in stony ground;
It sprang up in a moment,
Yet it could not grow;
Beneath the heat of the dawn
It began to wither away;
Leave me not, O Lord,
Lest in like manner I perish.

Cause me to grow in Thy vineyard,
That my fruit may abound;
I would follow in Thy way,
Grant me Thy grace, O Lord.
I long to feel in my soul
That Thou helpest me to overcome;
Leave me not, O Lord,
Grant me ever Thy power.
